# EXEMPTIONS FOR THE PUBLICATION COMPLETENESS CONTRACT.
#
# `.publication-boundary` declares that this repository gets published, and it
# switches on BOTH contracts: the leak guards (may this leave?) and
# engine/scripts/publication-completeness.sh (is everything that must be there,
# there, and usable by someone who has only the public repo?). This file adds
# no adoption switch and no thresholds. It carries deliberate, committed,
# reviewable exemptions and nothing else.
#
# WHY AN ESCAPE HATCH AT ALL
# --------------------------
# The same reason the boundary has an ALLOWLIST and no override token: a check
# with no sanctioned way through gets removed whole, and then protects nothing.
# So the way through is a line in a committed file, reviewed in a diff, with a
# reason written next to it — never an in-the-moment judgement call, which is
# the exact thing both contracts exist to replace.
#
# WHY THAT IS SAFE
# ----------------
#   AN ENTRY THAT SUPPRESSES NOTHING IS A FAILURE.
#
# Every exemption list is a place drift hides: the line was written for a real
# reason, the reason was fixed, and the line stayed — silently licensing the
# next instance of the defect. So the checker FAILS on an entry that no longer
# suppresses anything and names it for deletion. An exemption here cannot
# outlive its own justification.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CITATION_EXEMPT — documents whose paths describe A DIFFERENT REPOSITORY.
#
# Check 1 requires every path a public document cites to resolve in the public
# tree. That is right for a document describing THIS repository and wrong for a
# document describing the adopter's. These four trees are the latter, and each
# is template material by construction rather than by opinion:
#
#   engine/reference/      Its own README already says so, in prose: "Cross-file
#                          path references still point at the original layout and
#                          will not resolve here — that is expected for reference
#                          material." This line makes that existing declaration
#                          machine-readable; it grants no new license.
#   engine/skills/         Skills instruct an agent working in the ADOPTER's repo
#                          (`scripts/railway-api.sh`), name files a skill's own
#                          run creates (`.claude/product-marketing-context.md`,
#                          `ceo-wiki/wiki/vision-and-positioning.md`), and cite
#                          UPSTREAM provenance for vendored skills
#                          (`skills/taste-skill/SKILL.md` @ 72e2995).
#   engine/.claude/agents/ Agent definitions are the adopter's team. They name
#                          the adopter's own entry points (`scripts/preflight.sh`).
#   engine/qa-audits/      EXAMPLE_AUDIT.md is a shape to copy; its evidence
#                          screenshots are the adopter's, taken during their audit.
#
# THE COST, stated rather than discovered: a genuinely dangling citation inside
# one of these four trees is not caught. That is the price of the precision —
# without these, the check reported 26 findings of which 16 were correct
# documents doing their job, and a check that is 60% noise gets switched off.
CITATION_EXEMPT="engine/reference/ engine/skills/ engine/.claude/agents/ engine/qa-audits/"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT IS NOT IN THIS FILE, AND WHY IT LEFT
#
# A fourth key, INSTANCE_MECHANISMS, used to sit here. It named an executable
# inside the private sibling repository — a one-off verification script that
# reads a public contract and is correctly not published — so that Check 4
# would not report it as a capability withheld from the customer.
#
# It made this gate mean two different things:
#
#   ON THE MACHINE THAT WROTE IT the private tree resolved, Check 4 ran, the
#   entry suppressed a real finding, and the gate was green.
#
#   IN A CLONE OF THIS REPOSITORY ALONE — which is every CI runner, every
#   contributor and every reader — no private tree resolves, so Check 4 never
#   ran, the entry therefore suppressed nothing, and the rule directly above
#   fired and turned the gate red over a file that is not in this repository.
#
# The rule was right both times. What was wrong was judging an exemption
# belonging to a check that had not run — and, secondarily, publishing the
# interior layout of a private repository in the one file the boundary contract
# is supposed to keep honest.
#
#       A VERDICT ON THIS TREE MAY NOT DEPEND ON WHAT ELSE IS ON THE DISK.
#
# So the excuse moved to where the thing it excuses lives. A private mechanism
# that is one operator's artifact rather than a withheld capability now carries
#
#       instance-mechanism: <why this is one operator's artifact>
#
# in its own body, in the private repository, reviewed in that repository's own
# diff — the discipline `dialect-exempt: <reason>` already uses here. A bare
# marker with no reason after it exempts nothing, and a marker on a file that
# couples to no public contract is itself reported as a stale exemption, so it
# cannot outlive its reason either.
#
# WHAT THAT LEAVES IS A PROPERTY, not a fixed instance: every key this file
# still accepts is a function of `git ls-files` and the tracked bytes, so its
# verdict is the same in every clone. INSTANCE_MECHANISMS is refused by name
# with the migration if it reappears; it is not quietly ignored.
